\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Canada \highlight\uc2  dlr ends at 2-year low despite  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 482 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 April 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FORECAST RANGE   1.3850/1.3895\tab     ASIAN CLOSE     1.3850\par RESISTANCE 1.3740   SUPPORT 1.3925\tab HI 1.3865   LO  1.3840\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CANADA OPEN  1.3840/50    HI 1.3925     EUROPE OPEN     1.3843\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  PREV CLOSE   1.3883/88    LO 1.3841     HI 1.3852   LO  1.3842 \par \par \uc2  ----------------------MARKET COMMENT-------------------------- \par \par \uc2  * Canada's dollar ended weaker at C$1.3925 (US$0.7181) on \par \par \uc2  Thursday from Wednesday's close of C$1.3850 (US$0.7220) \par \par \uc2  despite \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  around the C$1.3910 \par \par \uc2  (US$0.7189) level. \par \par \uc2  * Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit its weakest level since April 4, 1995 under pressure from international investors calling for a rise in interest rates to match one by the Fed. \par \par \uc2  Traders said one major investor bought US$900 million worth of U.S. treasury bills from the Bank of Canada as others rushed out of Canadian short-term debt to take advantage of the 250 basis point spread between Canadian and U.S. yields. \par \par \uc2  Analysts pointed out that since the Federal Reserve moved last week the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has fallen nearly one U.S. cent from its C$1.3783 (US$0.7255) close on March 25. \par \par \uc2  Gregory said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could test levels as weak as C$1.4200 (US$0.7042) and beyond if the Bank of Canada resists the pressure for higher interest rates and fails to ratify market expections. \par \par \uc2  "Ratify me baby, ratify me," Gregory said. \par \par \uc2  Traders and analysts said all eyes will be focused on the U.S. non-farm payrolls report for March, due out on Friday at 0830 EST/1330 GMT. \par \par \uc2  A Reuter survey of economists forecast payrolls to be up 196,000 in March and have said a rise above that could provide further evidence of inflationary pressure in the U.S. economy and increase the likelihood the Fed will raise rates again at the next Federal Open Market Committee meeting in May. \par \par \uc2  Gregory said the Bank of Canada needs to raise rates to prove that it is no longer prepared to ease monetary conditions. \par \par \uc2  Economists said the Bank of Canada's resistance to higher rates could place the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the same position it was in at the start of 1995, when its brief resistance a rise in U.S. rates led to a speculative run against Canada's dollar. \par \par \uc2  Ultimately the Bank of Canada was forced to raise rates sharply in 1995 as a result, arguably placing the economy at risk of recession. \par \par \uc2  The mid-point of the Bank of Canada's 50 basis point target range for the overnight rate currently is 3.00 percent or 250 basis points below the 5.50 percent Federal funds rate in the U.S. \par \par \uc2  ((Paul Casciato, Reuters Toronto Bureau 416 941-8100 or email: paul.casciato@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt4307upq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
