\par\par \b \uc2  Heat on Bank of Canada to prop up weak dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Paul Simao \par \uc2 555 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 April 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TORONTO, April 2 (Reuter) - Canada's bleeding dollar will remain in intensive care unless the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to match a recent U.S. interest rate hike, economists said on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar weakened past the key C$1.3900 (US$0.7194) level this week, setting off another round of speculation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would raise its key bank rate by 25 basis points to shore up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not raised its key bank rate, which currently sits at a 35-year-low of 3.25 percent, since February 1995. \par \par \uc2  "What we have to see is the Bank of Canada actually signalling to markets that monetary conditions should be moving on a slightly tighter track," said Michael Gregory, economist and strategist with Lehman Brothers. \par \par \uc2  Gregory said he expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to raise rates within the next week. \par \par \uc2  A Canadian rate hike would match a similar move by the U.S. Federal Reserve. Last week, Fed Chairman Alan Greenspan raised U.S. rates 25 basis points in a pre-emptive strike amid signs of creeping U.S. inflation. \par \par \uc2  If U.S. growth continued its torrid pace, Greenspan would likely raise rates again when the Fed meets in May -- a move that could spell the end of the Bank of Canada's so-called "made-in-Canada" interest rate policy. \par \par \uc2  That policy refers to Bank of Canada Governor Gordon Thiessen's decision in 1995 to lower Canadian interest rates even while U.S. interest rates were unchanged. \par \par \uc2  "Markets clearly view last week's (U.S.) rate hike as the first in a series of Fed tightenings," said Stephen Wateridge, managing director of corporate \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  for CIBC Wood Gundy. \par \par \uc2  The widening of the spread between Canadian and U.S. interest rates to 225 basis points has already triggered a stampede of Canada-dollar selling in overseas markets. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar has lost more than 3.0 percent of its value against the U.S. dollar in the past two months. \par \par \uc2  Only domestic corporate buying of Canada dollars and some recent interest by Canadian exporters to hold the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had stemmed a further collapse of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Wateridge said. \par \par \uc2  The steady erosion of the dollar flies in the face of Canada's relatively strong economic fundamentals, which had been expected to help underpin the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a crisis. \par \par \uc2  Canada's economy was expected to grow more than 3.0 percent in 1997, while inflation should remain within the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target range of 1.0-3.0 percent, according to a Reuters poll of economists. \par \par \uc2  But jittery equity markets and controversy surrounding junior mining company Bre-X Minerals Ltd have added to the interest rate pressure on the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Speculation that Bre-X's Indonesian gold mine may contain much less gold than previously reported has set off a selling frenzy in mining stocks on the Toronto Stock Exchange. \par \par \uc2  Thiessen, however, appears unfazed by the bellowing for a quick interest rate strike. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Canada has more room to maneuver now than it did before, but that should not be interpreted as a pledge not to raise interest rates, Thiessen recently told reporters. \par \par \uc2  ((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt4207t4i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
