\par\par \b \uc2  World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -3: Official Suport For Peseta, Lira \b0\par\par\uc2 339 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1997\par 22:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  In other developments, the strength of the mark against its European counterparts triggered repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling of marks for the Spanish peseta and Italian lira overnight in Europe, traders there said. \par \par \uc2  'The bulk of the damage was done overnight,' said Jay Wertheimer, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at Banco di Sicilia in New York. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the Bank of Italy sold marks at about ITL1,003.50, after earlier - unsuccessful - attempts to defend the psychologically important level of ITL1,000. \par \par \uc2  Once Italy's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began selling at around ITL1003.50, however, the mark's rise was capped. 'We hit a hit a wall there,' one trader said. 'That quickly pushed it down to ITL1002.50.' \par \par \uc2  A dealer in Europe said Spain's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on at least three occasions to hold the mark below PES85.00. The Bank of Spain wouldn't comment on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rumors. \par \par \uc2  Observers said it wasn't clear whether the reported \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Italian and Spanish central banks would stop the momentum against the Mediterranean \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Players long on lira and pesetas could only sit and wait to see what the central banks do next, they noted, and the poor performance of most of Europe' bond markets does not provide much direction either. \par \par \uc2  'A lot of people don't know what to buy right now with all the uncertainty over EMU,' a trader said. \par \par \uc2  In other \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  was said to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market just after 1900 GMT (14:00 EST), selling U.S. dollars between C$1.3720 and C$1.3725. The move was in keeping with the bank's unofficial policy of grappling with sharp \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swings in a single session. \par \par \uc2  Canada's short-term interest rates, already below those in the U.S., are under pressure from heightening expectations that the Fed will soon raise U.S. interest rates. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 17-03-97 \par \par \uc2  2158GMT \par \par \uc2  1033 1865 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt3h01wk7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
