\par\par \b \uc2  Canadian Afternoon: Cdn Dlr Weakens, Causing Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 305 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1997\par 22:02\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (AP-Dow Jones)--Fear of a near-term hike to U.S. interest rates and selling on Chicago's International Monetary Market (IMM) sent the Canadian dollar tumbling Monday, prompting \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was trading at C$1.3709 at 3:28 a.m. EST (2028 GMT) up from C$1.3666 at 8:00 a.m. EST (1300 GMT), and from C$1.3650 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  But it hit a high at C$1.3728, just above levels at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began selling it in attempt to slow its rise (\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  began around C$1.3720 at about 2:00 p.m. EST). Unofficially, the bank tends to lean against intraday moves in excess of 70 ticks. \par \par \uc2  'It was a combination of U.S. rate concerns and interest on the IMM to sell (Canada) that caused the weakness,' said a dealer with a major Canadian bank. \par \par \uc2  Canada's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is highly vulnerable at the moment to an independent rate hike by the Fed - Canadian short-term interest rates are already well below their U.S. counterparts and the gap would only widen if U.S. rates are raised. \par \par \uc2  Many analysts expect the Bank of Canada initially to resist matching a Fed move, which few doubt will bring the Canadian dollar under pressure. \par \par \uc2  Eventually, however, analysts think the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have to raise its own rates. Stephen Poloz, managing editor at The International Bank Credit Analyst, reckons the bank will tighten policy should the U.S. dollar get up around the C$1.3850 area. (see story on page 32519 for an analysis). \par \par \uc2  Poloz was formerly the chief of research at the Bank of Canada. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 17-03-97 \par \par \uc2  2102GMT \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt3h01wfn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
