\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Canada \highlight\uc2  Afternoon: Dollar Slide Prompts Bank  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 295 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Februar 1997\par 22:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (AP-Dow Jones)--The Canadian dollar was off sharply late Wednesday against the U.S. dollar, a move that prompted the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its defense earlier in the session. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was trading at C$1.3665 at 4:28 p.m. EST (2128 GMT) Wednesday, up from C$1.3605 at 8:00 a.m. EST (1300 GMT), and up from C$1.3595 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Traders in Toronto said the sell-off began after comments from Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan just after 10 a.m. EST (1500 GMT) and the slide continued until \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . '\b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  just took it on the chin-that's all,' said a trader with a Canadian bank. \par \par \uc2  Dealers confirmed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began selling U.S. dollars around the C$1.3665 level and later around the C$1.3675 level, in keeping with the bank's unofficial policy of selling into \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves that exceed 70 ticks in either direction over the previous session. The U.S. dollar closed Tuesday around C$1.3595. \par \par \uc2  In his semi-annual Humphrey Hawkins address Greenspan suggested the U.S. economy remains strong enough to warrant caution toward inflation and implied a preemptive rise in official interest rates is a possibility. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. economy has shown few signs of inflation but the Chairman remained cautious keeping the Fed on 'alert' for any imbalance that might disrupt economic expansion. \par \par \uc2  The problem for Canadian investments is that interest rates north of the border are already lower than in the U.S.. A larger gap would likely make Canadian investments that much less attractive than their U.S counterparts. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 26-02-97 \par \par \uc2  2130GMT \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt2q01dn4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
