\par\par \b \uc2  Canadian Morning: Cdn Dlr Rallies Prompting BoC  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 383 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Januar 1997\par 15:55\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (AP-Dow Jones)--The Canadian dollar is sharply stronger against the U.S. dollar early Wednesday compared to levels late Tuesday, confounding some market participants with its rally and prompting the Bank of Canada to step in to slow the decline. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was trading at a session low of C$1.3427 at 9:55 a.m. EST (1455 GMT), down from C$1.3450 at 8:00 a.m. EST (1300 GMT), and C$1.3521 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Traders attributed a story in London's Financial Times for the Canadian dollar's rally, which started in Europe. Entitled 'Canada's soaraway economy', the article highlights the bullish attitudes many economists have about the Canadian economy and the Canadian dollar. \par \par \uc2  'People are jumping on the strong-growth bandwagon,' said Mark Chandler, senior economist at Goldman Sachs Canada, whose own firm is overweight the Canadian bond market based on assumptions the Canadian dollar will rise about 5% against the U.S. dollar this year. \par \par \uc2  'It's what everybody's been saying over here for the past three months,' added a dealer at a domestic bank in Toronto. 'But now the FT has said it, you can buy Canada.' \par \par \uc2  There had been some concern that the Canadian dollar's decline late Tuesday meant further weakness overnight. \par \par \uc2  Instead, the Canadian dollar rose so sharply traders said the Bank of England was selling Canadian dollars on behalf of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight to slow down the rise. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was continued by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  itself during Toronto time, as traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen buying U.S. dollars around C$1.3440 and are likely to continue throughout the morning. \par \par \uc2  Traders also said a strong performance by the U.S. dollar against some overseas \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  is attracting capital flows into North America, some of which are ending up in the Canadian dollar. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par These are the exchange rates at 9:55 a.m. EST (1455 GMT) Wednesday\par 8:00 a.m. EST (1300 GMT) and late Tuesday.\par    U.S./CDN    1.3427      1.3450    1.3521\par    CDN/DEM     1.1872      1.1888    1.1789\par    CDN/YEN     87.33       87.31     86.50\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 15-01-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1455GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt1f008kk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
