\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Futures -2: Trading Heavy In CAD, AUD \b0\par\par\uc2 391 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Januar 1997\par 22:22\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, strength in the U.S. dollar led to weakness for much of the day in the British pound and only furthered a major slide in the Australian dollar, some dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Declining gold prices and a slew of weak economic data were among other factors, as were unfounded rumors, eventually quashed by the Reserve Bank, that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board would ease monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  But the U.S. dollar's strength did benefit the Canadian dollar, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rallied fervently for the second straight day, attracting \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise. \par \par \uc2  Market observers said the bank stepped in just around C$1.3495 to C$1.3500 "to touch it" a bit and remind the market that the Bank of Canada often steps in whenever the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves more than 70 ticks in either direction in a single session, leaning against it to discourage excessive volatility. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar closed Tuesday around C$1.3567, and was testing below C$1.3500 around 1845 GMT. It hit a low at C$1.3493 at 1859 GMT and the bank moved in a short time after that. \par \par \uc2  On the IMM, the Canadian dollar futures contract had a "tripple bottom around 74.10 cents, dipped underneath and bounced pretty good," according to one trader there. Volume was heavy at 13,000 contracts, second in volume only to mark contracts. \par \par \uc2  Three U.S. brokerages bought a total of 2,000 March Canadian dollar futures at various prices. \par \par \uc2  One Wall Street investment bank sold 2,500 March Mexican pesos futures between 12.3450 and 12.3300 cents and another Wall Street bank bought 1,000 of them. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Other contracts traded as follows:\par    MARCH CONTRACT        LEVEL         CHANGE\par    Australian Dlr       77.95 cents    Dn 0.97\par    Canadian Dlr         74.33 cents    Up 0.31\par    Swiss Franc          73.76 cents    Up 0.62\par    Mexican Peso         12.3325        Up 0.0250\par    French franc         18.880         Dn 0.140\par    Brazil real    (Feb.)0.95470        Dn 0.0003\par    FINEX Dlr Index      89.45          Up 0.44\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar was trading at 1.5740 marks and 115.75 yen, up from 1.5639\par marks and from 115.20 yen late Tuesday in New York.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) DOW JONES NEWS 01-08-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1622EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1049 1846 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dt18000oy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
