\par\par \b \uc2  Canadian Afternoon: Cdn Dlr Soars Prompting BoC To Slow Rise \b0\par\par\uc2 411 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Januar 1997\par 23:02\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Canadian dollar ended Tuesday's session\par significantly stronger against the U.S. dollar compared with\par Monday's levels, as heavy demand for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  prompted the Bank\par of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to limit the Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rise.\par    The U.S. dollar was trading at C$1.3560 at 2145 GMT, down from\par C$1.3610 at 1300 GMT and C$1.3655 late Monday.\par    "The Canadian dollar seems in play," said one trader at a U.S.\par bank in New York. "And it seems a lot of people got on board."\par    The Canadian dollar has staged a remarkable recovery since\par falling sharply early in last Friday's session. Then, the U.S.\par dollar hit a high against the Canada of around C$1.3780. But the\par fortunes of the U.S. dollar quickly turned, and it ended the week on\par a downward note, fueled by selling of the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by European\par investment funds.\par    The U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  unit's collapse accelerated Monday and was given a\par further push down Tuesday after a buy recommendation on the Canadian\par dollar was issued out of London by the global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par department of Deutsche Morgan Grenfell. The firm believes the\par Canadian economy is set to recover, and the Bank of Canada may have\par to raise interest rates at some point\par - likely in the second quarter.\par    The rise of the Canadian dollar has been so quick over the past\par few days that the Bank of Canada was forced into the market to try\par and slow down its ascent. Traders said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was buying\par U.S. dolars Tuesday at C$1.3575/80. The U.S. unit fell to its\par session low of C$1.3556 at 1811 GMT.\par    Al Merz, director of institutional sales and trading at TD\par Securities Inc in New York, said the magnitude of the move down by\par the U.S. dollar means there have been some big sellers of the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and buyers of the Canadian dollar over the last couple of\par sessions.\par    "This move back is very healthy for the Canadian dollar." he\par said.\par    These are the exchange rates at 2145 GMT Tuesday, 1300 GMT and\par late Monday.\par    U.S./CDN    1.3560      1.3610    1.3655\par    CDN/DEM     1.1538      1.1474    1.1453\par    CDN/YEN     84.98       84.74     84.77\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) DOW JONES NEWS 01-07-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1702EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4020 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dt17004a7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
