\par\par \b \uc2  J.P. Morgan/Cdn Bonds -2: End Of Rate Cutting Cited \b0\par\par\uc2 345 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Januar 1997\par 21:54\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  "Canada was a really good story," said Prins at J.P. Morgan, referring to the autumn of 1996. Canada's 10-year bond yield fell from about 7% in early October to about 6% by early December. The U.S. dollar fell from well over C$1.3700 in the late summer to a 1996-low at C$1.3280 in early November. \par \par \uc2  But through December both bonds and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  suffered sharp losses, partly as global investors took big profits on the run up in October and November. \par \par \uc2  And at the same time, the Canadian economic indicators began to show clear signs of recovery and U.S. data started to point at a renewal of the robust figures seen earlier in the year. Many analysts began suggesting the Bank of Canada would no longer need to lower interest rates, while the Federal Reserve might be forced to raise U.S. rates. \par \par \uc2  Canada's 10-year bond yield surged and is now trading at 6.66%. On Friday, the U.S. dollar peaked just under C$1.3800, after a two-month run-up against the Canadian dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has since begun an impressive recovery, reaching a low around C$1.3556 this session, a move sharp enough to prompt the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice with selling in an effort to cool its rise. \par \par \uc2  But J.P. Morgan's U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  based its decision to lower the weighting recommendation on the previous action in the market, said Prins. \par \par \uc2  The fall rally in the Canadian markets was fueled as the Bank of Canada aggressively led short-term interest rates lower. Global investment houses steadily boosted their recommended weightings in Canadian bonds from the 3% neutral level as a result. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut the key overnight rate three times in October alone, following up with another one in the first week of November, taking interest rates to their lowest levels in decades. \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES NEWS 01-07-97 \par \par \uc2  1554EST \par \par \uc2  4020 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dt1700472\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
