\par\par \b \uc2  =Weak Canada Jobs Report Underscores Need For Easy Rates \b0\par\par\uc2  By Eric Van Zant \par \uc2 321 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Dezember 1996\par 15:14\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TORONTO (Dow Jones)--News that Canada's labor market\par remains unsteady, with just 7,000 new jobs created in\par November, confirms the need for stable to lower interest\par rates in coming months, economists said.\par    Statistics Canada reported Friday that the unemployment\par rate remained stubbornly high in November at 10%, the same\par as October. Full-time employment fell by 23,000 jobs and was\par only offset by 30,000 new positions in the part-time area.\par    The only bright spot, said economists, was a strong\par addition of 44,000 jobs in the service sector.\par    But the manufacturing and construction areas, which many\par had expected would show greater strength, actually weakened.\par Employment in the goods-producing industries declined by\par 11,000 in November.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    "It shows the economy is struggling to regain a stronger\par pace of growth and it will probably keep the Bank of Canada\par in an accomodative mode, which obviously could threaten the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the markets at least temporarily," said Aron\par Gampel, deputy chief economist at ScotiaBank.\par    The figures couldn't have come at a more uncertain time,\par with bonds registering their biggest two-day loss in over a\par decade on Wednesday and Thursday. Since early November,\par meanwhile, the U.S. dollar has climbed nearly 2.5% against\par the Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to trade around C$1.3600. The speed of\par the decline in the Canadian dollar prompted the Bank of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  twice in the Canadian dollar's support\par this week.\par    Markets got some respite from news earlier Friday that\par the U.S. economy created just 118,000 non-farm jobs in\par November, well below forecasts. But the economists worry that\par talk of need for further Canadian rate cuts could keep the\par Canadian dollar under pressure and thereby actually force a\par defensive rate hike from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) DOW JONES NEWS 12-06-96\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0914EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4230 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011013dsc602x4l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
