ts at 121.57 and yields 7.2%, up from 6.89% late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  But the move also occurs after rallying sharply over the last couple months. Players holding long Canadian dollar positions are taking the opportunity going into the end of the year to unload and take profits, traders said. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 05-12-96 \par \par \uc2  1651GMT \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011014dsc501koa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
