\par\par \b \uc2  Canada Bonds -2: Investors Scrambling To Protect Profits \b0\par\par\uc2 322 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Dezember 1996\par 18:04\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    TORONTO (Dow Jones)--Canadian bonds continue to be hit\par by massive selling at mid-morning Thursday, with the 30-year\par bond down more than four points in one of the worst one-day\par selloffs since April 1994.\par    While a number of factors are behind the scramble by\par investors to protect their profits, the weakness of the\par Canadian dollar is a key factor.\par    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market players said the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  all morning in an effort to stem the decline in\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against the U.S. dollar - but so far to little\par avail. The U.S. dollar soared to C$1.3614 at 1620 GMT, but\par Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  selling has pulled it back down below\par the C$1.36 level.\par    6.25s 1998 103.00  dn 1.03  4.45% vs 3.86%\par    7.0s  2001 105.00  dn 2.12  5.75% vs 5.26%\par    7.0s  2006 102.90  dn 2.90  6.59% vs 6.20%\par    9s    2025 121.80  dn 4.33  7.18% vs 6.89%\par    10-Yr Spread To U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  10-Yr:  0.39 vs  0.11\par    CGB Mar 97 115.70  dn 2.71  volume 5,269\par    "There's no fundamental factor behind the fall in\par bonds," said Arve Bendiksrud, fixed-income analyst at TD\par Securities. "People are trying to protect their substantial\par profits."\par    While there may have been some foreign selling that\par kicked things off, Bendiksrud said volumes have been heavy\par and domestic players have been very active in the market\par Thursday.\par    He and other analysts resisted making any calls on when\par this rout will end, but many believe there will be a bounce\par back from the massive selloff since Canadian bonds are now\par cheaper than they were, with a cheaper \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the\par fundamental story still remains positive for Canada.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) DOW JONES NEWS 12-05-96\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1204EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4020 4152 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011013dsc502vqg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
