\par\par \b \uc2  =Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada Intervenes \highlight\uc2  In  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Mkt To Protect Low Rates \b0\par\par\uc2  By Michael McHugh \par \uc2 342 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 1996\par 23:11\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TORONTO (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Monday to try to stabilize a weakening\par Canadian dollar in order to preserve the country's low\par interest rates for a while longer, economists said.\par    Since hitting year highs in early November, the Canadian\par dollar has been steadily losing ground. But until now, there\par has been little reaction in the country's financial markets.\par In fact, short- and long-term interest rates generally have\par been falling in anticipation of another interest-rate cut by\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    But Monday, in response to the weak Canadian dollar, bond\par and bill markets sold off. The 30-year bond was off almost a\par full point at its worst point. By late Monday, the 30-year\par bond recovered somewhat, ending the day down 0.63, pushing\par the yield up four basis points to 6.76%. The yield on the\par three-month bill meanwhile fell three basis points to 2.76%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    "The bank wants to defend the low interest-rate regime\par that it's built up, and today showed the first signs of some\par skittishness in the bills market in response to the weakening\par of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said Avery Shenfeld, senior economist at\par CIBC Wood Gundy Securities Inc.\par    The U.S. dollar rose to a high Monday of around C$1.3545\par before the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  came in and began selling U.S.\par dollars in favor of Canadian dollars. That dragged the U.S.\par dollar down to a low of around C$1.3496 before it bounced\par back to around C$1.3505 currently.\par    "This is one of those instances when they felt it would\par be useful to step in and provide a little bit of guidance to\par the market," said Ted Carmichael, senior economist at J.P.\par Morgan Securities Canada. "It was an indication that a steady\par depreciation in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is probably not what the bank\par thinks is appropriate."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) DOW JONES NEWS 12-02-96\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1711EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1196 4264 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011013dsc202v6f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
