\par\par \b \uc2  Bank of Canada cuts key interest rate to 3.50 percent. \b0\par\par\uc2 233 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Oktober 1996\par 16:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  OTTAWA, Oct. 28 (Reuter) - The Bank of Canada on Monday cut its key bank rate to 3.50 percent from 3.75 percent, the lowest short-term interest rate Canada has seen in 36 years. \par \par \uc2  The move quickly prompted five of Canada's six major chartered banks to lower their prime lending rates to 5.0 percent from 5.25 percent, their lowest level since July 1956. \par \par \uc2  The bank rate, which has changed in nature over past decades, is now at its lowest level since August 1963. \par \par \uc2  It was the 10th rate cut this year by the Bank of Canada, and the 19th since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began easing in May 1995. The Bank of Canada has now cut rates by 475 basis points since May 1995 in a bid to jump-start \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sluggish economy. \par \par \uc2  Through direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the money market, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dropped its target range for the overnight lending rate to 3.0-3.50 percent from 3.25-3.75 percent. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Canada uses the bank rate for loans it gives to financial institutions as lender of last resort. It is the top of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target range for the overnight rate. \par \par \uc2  Canadian Treasury bills firmed after the rate cut, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and bonds traded steady. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018dsas0167z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
