\par\par \b \uc2  Canada Bonds -2: Mkt Focus To Be On U.S. CPI, Bank of Canada \b0\par\par\uc2 303 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Oktober 1996\par 22:01\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The yield on the three-month treasury bill fell early,\par but is ending the session only off three basis points to\par yield 3.41%. At the present level, the rate is below the\par bottom end of the bank's target between 3.5% and 4% -\par following a pattern that sees the market take rates down\par first and then the bank ratifying the move with a rate cut.\par    Although the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  failed to cut rates at its\par normal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  time, the release of\par weaker-than-expected inflation figures in the U.S. pushed\par U.S. Treasurys higher. Canadian prices moved up in tandem.\par    The Labor Department said the producer price index rose\par 0.2%, down from expectations of a gain of 0.3%, further\par bolstering the U.S. Federal Reserve's decision last month to\par keep interest rates steady, economists said.\par    Focus for the markets next week will be Wednesday's U.S.\par consumer price index report. There will also be\par manufacturing data out of Canada Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Underpining the economic reports, however, will be the\par threat of a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate cut. The bank last lowered its\par rate Oct. 2, using a rising Canadian dollar to justify the\par reduction in rates. The Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is above levels\par seen earlier in the month, as the U.S. dollar ended Friday\par around C$1.3512 after being around C$1.36 at the time of the\par last rate cut.\par    Analysts expect the Canadian dollar to continue rising,\par and that should heighten the anticipation of action by the\par Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    Meanwhile, the Quebec National Assembly resumes sitting\par Tuesday, and details of the Oct. 23 30-year auction will be\par released Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) DOW JONES NEWS 10-11-96\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1601EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4152 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011013dsab02f08\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
