\par\par \b \uc2  Canadian Afternoon: Cdn Dlr Ends Tumultuous Session Lower \b0\par\par\uc2 335 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juli 1996\par 21:05\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (AP-Dow Jones)--The Canadian dollar ended a tumultuous session lower Friday, hurt early by a surprising drop in employment in June that triggered speculation of a Bank of Canada rate cut. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was trading at C$1.3684 at 1900 GMT, up from C$1.3633 at 1230 GMT and C$1.3589 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened dramatically after Statistics Canada said the economy shed 56,000 jobs in June. That came after a 12,000 drop in May. \par \par \uc2  The weakness in the economy added more fuel to fears the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may try to cut its overnight lending rate from the current band of between 4.5% and 5% - particularly after the U.S. Federal Reserve chose to keep its key lending rate steady Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  'We've seen a fairly negative reaction to the unemployment numbers,' said John Nicholson, managing director of global \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at Scotia Capital Markets. \par \par \uc2  With the drop in jobs, and the 36,000 rise in the labor force, Canada's unemployment rate rose to 10% - its highest point since October 1994. \par \par \uc2  Compounding problems for the Canadian dollar was the robust growth in U.S. jobs last month. The U.S. Labor Department said non-farm payrolls rose 239,000 in June - substantially higher than consensus estimates of 150,000. \par \par \uc2  'That will lead to higher interest rates in the U.S., and obviously that won't be the situation in Canada - and the (Canadian) \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will suffer in the near term because of that,' said Nicholson. \par \par \uc2  After the 1100 GMT release of the Canadian data, the U.S. dollar shot up to its session high of C$1.37 at 1340 GMT. The strong move up in the U.S. dollar prompted the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and sell U.S. dollars into the rally starting around the C$1.3665 level. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 05-07-96 \par \par \uc2  1905GMT \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds7505jms\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
