\par\par \b \uc2  Canadian Mid-Morning: Cdn Dlr Recovers From Earlier Losses \b0\par\par\uc2 243 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juli 1996\par 17:25\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (AP-Dow Jones)--The Canadian dollar has recovered slightly from earlier heavy losses Friday, bolstered by supportive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  and renewed buying from investors. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was trading at C$1.3682 at 1508 GMT, up from C$1.3602 at 0930 GMT and C$1.3589 late Thursday. It hit a high at C$1.3700. Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began selling U.S. dollars at C$1.3665 and was heavily selling up to the session's high. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  plunged early against the U.S. dollar amid speculation that huge job losses in the Canadian labor market would push the Bank of Canada to lower short-term interest rates again. \par \par \uc2  The key overnight rate currently trades in a target band between 4.50-5.00% and was last lowered 1/4 point on April 18. \par \par \uc2  Statistics Canada said the economy lost 56,000 jobs in June compared with expectations of a gain of anywhere from 15,000 to 40,000. Economists were expecting a rebound from the 12,000 jobs lost in May. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar's losses accelerated after news the U.S. economy added another 239,000 non-farm jobs in June, raising anticipation of a U.S. rate hike in August and the specter of divergent North American monetary policies. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 05-07-96 \par \par \uc2  1525GMT \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds7505jf3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
