\par\par \b \uc2  Canada Bonds Fall, As U.S. Jobs Override Weak Cdn Data \b0\par\par\uc2 358 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juli 1996\par 22:17\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TORONTO (Dow Jones)--Canadian bonds tumbled Friday,\par joining U.S. Treasurys in another post-employment report\par rout as a strong U.S. June payroll number refueled talk of\par the need for a rate hike south of the border.\par    Indeed, news the U.S. economy created 239,000 new\par non-farm jobs last month almost entirely superceded\par reports from Statistics Canada of large job losses in the\par Canadian economy. The domestic economy shed 56,000 jobs in\par June.\par    Canadian bonds outperformed U.S. Treasurys this\par session. But some analysts say that may only be because of\par expectations that the Canadian dollar won't suffer further\par given that the Bank of Canada will find it difficult to\par cut interest rates in the face of a U.S. rate hike.\par    6.0s  1998  99.80  dn 0.27  6.10% vs 5.93%\par    7.5s  2001 101.25  dn 0.74  7.16% vs 6.96%\par    7.00s 2006  93.78  dn 1.27  7.87% vs 7.68%\par    9s    2025 107.89  dn 1.95  8.27% vs 8.10%\par    CGB Sept   106.77  dn 1.33  Volume 4,422\par    10-Yr Spread To U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  10-Yr: 0.82 vs 0.92\par    "It's because the Bank of Canada didn't ease today\par that we were able to sustain tighter spreads," said Robert\par Palombi, fixed-income analyst with MMS International.\par    After the jobs report, many thought the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par would quickly lower interest rates, and the Canadian\par dollar tumbled in response. It's feared the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  can't\par weather divergent U.S. and Canadian monetary policies, as\par the two jobs reports suggest would be required.\par    The U.S. dollar hit a high at C$1.3700 shortly after\par the Statscan report, up from levels below C$1.3600 late\par Thursday. The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Canada intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to sell U.S.\par dollars starting around C$1.3665.\par    Spreads in the bond market narrowed substantially,\par with the 10-year spread over the U.S. Treasury down 10\par basis points to 82 points.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) DOW JONES NEWS 07-05-96\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1617EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4152 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011013ds7501l02\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
