\par\par \b \uc2  World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -4: Brighter EMU Prospects Pressure Mark \b0\par\par\uc2 283 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 April 1996\par 00:52\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Traders in Europe, but not in New York, said the mark was also pressured Monday by a renewed sense of optimism about the European single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's timetable. \par \par \uc2  Friday, the European Union (E.U.) convened a year-long Inter-Governmental Conference in Turin, Italy, to discuss changes in E.U. institutions. \par \par \uc2  Although the European Economic and Monetary Union (EMU) isn't formally on the conference's agenda, some E.U. officials are already using the forum to reassure markets that EMU is still on track to begin in 1999. \par \par \uc2  Monetary union is often seen as negative for the mark, as markets are unlikely to have as much confidence in the EMU's euro, which will be weighed down by less stable European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as an anchor \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for Europe. \par \par \uc2  'I've heard a little talk about (EMU Monday), but not a lot,' said Goldman's Lopatin. 'Clearly, the progress of EMU is a big issue for the value of the mark,' particularly against other European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere Monday, the dollar weakened against its Canadian counterpart. Traders in Canada said the Canadian dollar got support from investors buying long-term Canadian bonds. \par \par \uc2  Late in New York Monday, the dollar was quoted at $1.3548 (Canadian), down from C$1.3591 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent strengthening has worried some traders that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  will either \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow its rise or cut short-term interest rates again. The Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last cut its key lending rate March 21 by 0.25 percentage point to a band of 4.75%-5.00%. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 01-04-96 \par \par \uc2  2252GMT \par \par \uc2  1033 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds4102u05\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
