\par\par \b \uc2  Bank of Canada lowers rates independently of U.S.. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Jeffrey Hodgson \par \uc2 406 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1996\par 23:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TORONTO, March 21 (Reuter) - In a bid to boost the sluggish economy, the Bank of Canada Thursday cut key interest rates to below comparable U.S. rates for the first time in more than a year. \par \par \uc2  Canada's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut short-term rates independently of the U.S. Federal Reserve for the second time this year, a move that weakened the Canadian dollar. \par \par \uc2  "They bit the bullet and said we need lower rates," said Joshua Mendelsohn, chief economist with the Canadian Imperial Bank of Commerce. "There are some signs of improvement (in the economy) but it's still pretty sluggish." \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement that the relatively rare independent cut in domestic rates was consistent with the country's good inflation performance. \par \par \uc2  "The argument has always been that Canada's low inflation rate should allow it to have rates equal to or lower than the U.S., so you have that at work," said Mendelsohn. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also said the recent appreciation in the value of the Canadian dollar "contributed to a positive backdrop in financial markets for this move." \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the money market early Thursday to lower the centre of the target range for its overnight lending rate by a quarter point to 5.0 percent -- below the U.S. overnight bank lending rate, or federal funds rate, of 5.25 percent, for the first time since December 1994. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Canada had hesitated in reducing rates below similar U.S. rates because of concerns such a move would weaken the Canadian dollar. \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell only marginally after the rate cut, slipping to US$0.7342 from its open of US$0.7366. \par \par \uc2  "We have dropped interest rates remarkably and it hasn't had an adverse impact on our \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said John Kellett, vice-president of equities with Royal Bank of Canada. "(The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) has done very well." \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar has appreciated by almost 1 1/2 U.S. cents in the past month, providing room for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cut. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was strengthened by positive investor response to this month's federal budget, strong economic fundamentals, and recent comments by Quebec Premier Lucien Bouchard that a referendum on separation will be delayed until after a provincial election is held sometime before 1998. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019ds3l0012q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
