\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Canada Intervenes \highlight\uc2  -2: Seen As Smoothing  \highlight22\uc2 Operation \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 215 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Februar 1996\par 20:11\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (AP-DOW JONES)--Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday in support of the Canadian dollar, selling U.S. dollars around C$1.3795 at 1340 GMT. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar closed at C$1.3720 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  A dealer with a large Canadian bank said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  started to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  around the C$1.3795 level up to about C$1.3800. Another dealer with medium-sized Canadian investment bank said the same. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the Canadian dollar has come under pressure on concern that a raft of bonds maturing in the next couple weeks will see a significant portion of funds repatriated. The intevention was aimed at smoothing out the U.S. dollar's rise, they said. \par \par \uc2  Some C$2.6 billion in 10-year bonds, orginally auctioned in 1986, are due for redemption on March 1 and C$4.9 billion of 4.75% bonds originally launched in December 1993 will mature March 15. \par \par \uc2  Traders also expressed concern about a number of Euro-Canadian bond issues maturing in the next weeks. \par \par \uc2  Since the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the U.S. dollar has fallen back to about C$1.3790. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 14-02-96 \par \par \uc2  1911GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds2e01dg8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
