\par\par \b \uc2  Canadian Morning -2: Risks Seen In  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Policy \b0\par\par\uc2 360 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Februar 1996\par 16:20\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The upside risk now for the Canadian dollar is the likelihood that the Bank of Canada will use any sustained strength to cut interest rates again. 'The negatives are that the (bank) continues to pursue a very accomodative policy,' said Johnson. \par \par \uc2  On Jan. 25, the bank boldly lowered its target for overnight funds, independently of the U.S. Federal Reserve, risking a potential sell off in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and signalling a more agressive desire to ease monetary conditions in a sluggish Canadian economy. \par \par \uc2  However, when the Fed cut the following Wednesday, Jan. 31, the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was able to match it with another 1/4-point cut to overnight funds without unduly harming the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The overnight rate is now allowed to trade in a range between 5.00-5.50%. It currently trades at the mid-point of the range. \par \par \uc2  'But but i don't think that's necessarily that negative,' said Johnson. \par \par \uc2  The spectre of another unilateral rate cut rises with sustained strength in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  But analysts have said the move would be more risky because it would leave the mid-point for Canadian overnight money below the U.S. target for federal funds, currently 5.25%. \par \par \uc2  On another front, the sharp upturn in the Canadian dollar raises the potential for Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The bank's usual strategy is to smooth out any sharp movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and it normally will step in whenever the U.S. dollar moves up or down more than 70 ticks against the Canadian dollar in a session. \par \par \uc2  This session, that would mean if the U.S. dollar falls to around C$1.3650, traders will be on the look out for some selling of the Canadian dollar by the Bank of Canada to cool its rise. \par \par \uc2  These are the exchange rates at 1432 GMT Wednesday, at 1300 GMT and late Tuesday. U.S./CDN         1.3705   1.3697     1.3714 CDN/Mark         1.0761   1.0776     1.0726 CDN/Yen          77.38    77.45      76.65 \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 07-02-96 \par \par \uc2  1520GMT \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds27015mf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
