\par\par \b \uc2  Canadian Dlr -2: Fed Ease Would Spur C$ Rally \b0\par\par\uc2 243 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Januar 1996\par 22:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The concern in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets is that if the policy-making Federal Open Market Committee (FOMC) does not reduce U.S. rates, the Canadian dollar is likely in for more selling pressure. \par \par \uc2  The adjusted short-term interest-rate spread between Canada and the U.S. is hovering at 52-week lows of just above 10 basis points - a risk premium viewed as insufficient to retain foreign investors in Canada if the prospects for lower funding costs are wiped out. \par \par \uc2  Some anticipate the U.S. dollar could rise toward the C$1.40 level if the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decides to keep rates steady after its two-day meeting. 'The Fed has to ease before we can see a rally in the Canadian dollar,' said a trader. \par \par \uc2  Although the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  a couple of times Friday to help support the Canadian dollar, many market participants and economists believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is content with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the present weakened levels. \par \par \uc2  A lower \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , along with the lower interest rates, will provide a much-needed stimulus to the Canadian economy. \par \par \uc2  These are the exchange rates at 2015 GMT and at 1300 GMT Monday, and late Friday. U.S./CDN         1.3787   1.3794     1.3810 CDN/Mark         1.0753   1.0807     1.0786 CDN/Yen          77.44    77.24      77.12 \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 29-01-96 \par \par \uc2  2100GMT \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds1t00u72\par }