\par\par \b \uc2  Canadian Morning: Cdn Dlr Losses Prompt  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 318 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Januar 1996\par 16:48\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (AP-DJ)--The Canadian dollar was lower and under pressure in volatile early dealings Friday, prompting the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and sell U.S. dollars in its support. Thursday's unilateral rate cut by the bank has left the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  vulnerable to weakness. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was trading at C$1.3815 at 1537 GMT, up from C$1.3787 at 1300 GMT and C$1.3788 Thursday. \par \par \uc2  A trader with one of the large Canadian banks said the Bank of Canada began selling U.S. dollar around C$1.3825-30, while another dealer confirmed that the bank was heavily active in that area. \par \par \uc2  Thursday, the Bank of Canada lowered its target for overnight funds by 1/4 point to 5.25-5.75%, surprising many who had felt the bank would not cut rates independently of the Fed. (see story on page 4229) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials cited the recent drop in inflation in justifying the rate cut. Statistics Canada reported on Tuesday that consumer prices had risen 1.7% on an annualized basis in December, from 2.1% in November. That brings it below the midpoint of the Bank of Canada's 1-3% target range. \par \par \uc2  But the move puts the lower level of the overnight rate target under the current fed funds target at 5.50%. Historically, such a move has often led to a sharp sell off of the Canadian dollar, said observers. \par \par \uc2  An economist with PATH International, a market analytics firm, said the next target for the Canadian dollar is the June 13 high at C$1.3855. He noted that short-term interest rates have been relatively stable despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness, but said that further significant strength in the U.S. dollar will 'will see desks let go of bills.' \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 26-01-96 \par \par \uc2  1548GMT \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds1q00s5y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
