\par\par \b \uc2  Canadian Bonds Higher As Strong Cdn Dlr, Treasurys Boost Mkt \b0\par\par\uc2 363 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Dezember 1995\par 15:30\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (AP-DJ)--Canadian bonds opened higher Wednesday, boosted in a thin market by a strong Canadian dollar and higher U.S. Treasurys. Gains in the U.S. market were constrained with U.S. budget negotiations on hold until Friday when President Clinton is slated to meet with Rebublican congressional leaders. The government shutdown caused by the budget impasse has delayed the release of November durable goods orders scheduled for this session. But coupled with new highs in the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , strength in U.S. bonds has fueled the Canadian upturn begun last week after the U.S. Federal Reserve and Bank of Canada cut rates. 7s    1997 101.68 up 0.09   5.92% VS 5.99% 7.5s  2000 103.35 up 0.25   6.64% VS 6.69% 8.75s 2005 111.14 up 0.39   7.15% VS 7.28% 9s    2025 115.60 up 0.73   7.65% VS 7.76% CGB March  111.45 up 0.47   Volume 257 10-Yr Spread To U.S. \par \par \uc2   10-Yr 1.49 vs 1.52 Many traders are bridging the gap between the Christmas and New Year's holiday and desks are thinly staffed and flows light, said observers. But sentiment remains positive given the renewed hope for lower rates inspired by the Fed cut last Tuesday. "The curve has steepened significantly and the tone is very positive," said a dealer with a large Canadian bank. He said the uncertainty toward the U.S. market could tend to put a cap on the upside, but hopes are high for the rally to persist. Another test of resistance levels by the Canadian dollar only supports the market. It now gets US73.62 cents, up from around US73.44 cents late last week, established after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy U.S. dollars and slow the rise of the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders are wary of another appearance by the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 : some look for it to sell Canadian around US73.70 cents, but the tone will remain strong. \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES NEWS 12-27-95 \par \par \uc2  0930EST \par \par \uc2  4118 4152 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011024drcr02vvh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
