\par\par \b \uc2  Canadian Afternoon: Cdn Dlr Up, Stable After  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 385 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Dezember 1995\par 22:06\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (AP-DJ)--The Canadian dollar rallied through much of the Thursday session as professional traders played with technical levels in thin holiday flows, prompting the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice in an effort to slow its rise. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar is trading at C$1.3632 at 2047 GMT, down from C$1.3644 at 1300 GMT and C$1.3675 late Wednesday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen buying the U.S. dollar twice around the C$1.3600/05 level. \par \par \uc2  'It was thin markets and stops along the way - there was no huge business to suggest that a two (Canadian cent) move was justified,' said Diego Giurleo, vice president, treasury at the Royal Bank of Canada, explaining that the sharp gains of the past three sessions resulted as the Canadian dollar broke through key levels, triggering stop-loss orders and forcing traders to sell the U.S. dollar as it continued to fall. \par \par \uc2  'In thin markets, when stop levels are triggered, you hit vacuums - your next level could be significantly lower and that's what's caused this huge move in the Canada,' he said. \par \par \uc2  After the Federal Reserve cut rates Tuesday, immediately followed by the Bank of Canada, the Canadian dollar began rising. From levels around C$1.3780 just before the cut, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell nearly two Canadian cents to a low around C$1.3583 midday Thursday before stabilizing. \par \par \uc2  The Fed lowered its funds rate 1/4 point to 5.50%. The Bank of Canada matched that, bringing the call-loan target band to 5.50%-6.00%. \par \par \uc2  By cutting rates, the Fed gave the Bank of Canada much-needed breathing room to steer rates lower and provide the sagging Canadian economy some stimulus. Traders had feared that if the Fed didn't ease policy the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be forced to act alone, with negative implications for the Canadian dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Canada has made it clear that its role is not to stop the direction of the Canadian dollar at anytime. But 'its intentions were to mitigate any further volatility - it's done that and told the market that it's there,' said Giurleo. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 21-12-95 \par \par \uc2  2106GMT \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025drcl0aahr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
