\par\par \b \uc2  Bank of Canada Buying U.S. Dlrs Again; Stems Rally In C$ \b0\par\par\uc2 178 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Dezember 1995\par 20:17\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (AP-DJ)--The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets again Thursday, this time buying U.S. dollars around the C$1.3580-90 level. \par \par \uc2  Earlier in the day, traders said the bank was buying U.S. dollars at the C$1.36 level. But as the market tested the bank's resolve to let the U.S. dollar fall below that level again, the bank backed off and pulled their punches. \par \par \uc2  That tripped some stop/loss orders that pushed the U.S. dollar down toward to C$1.3580. That's when the bank stepped in and started buying around C$1.3582, C$1.3585 and C$1.3588. \par \par \uc2  One trader at a domestic bank said as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stopped the most recent decline in the U.S. dollar, a large U.S. buyer of U.S. dollars pushed the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  up to around C$1.3620. -0-. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 21-12-95 \par \par \uc2  1917GMT \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025drcl0aa6c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
