\par\par \b \uc2  Canadian Bonds Close Higher On Stronger Canadian Dollar \b0\par\par\uc2 370 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Dezember 1995\par 22:35\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (AP-DJ)--Canadian bonds ended Thursday's session higher, buoyed by a strong rally in the Canadian dollar that forced the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to limit the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise. But traders and analysts also said the Canadian market was very quiet, with many desks already in the holiday spirit. The middle section of the yield curve garnered a little more attention. Spreads between Canada and the U.S. tightened across the curve as the U.S. market ended mixed but did not stray too far from unchanged. 7s    1997 101.47 up 0.08   6.06% VS 6.12% 7.5s  2000 102.74 up 0.22   6.79% VS 6.85% 8.75s 2005 110.12 up 0.30   7.29% VS 7.36% 9s    2025 114.60 up 0.18   7.77% VS 7.79% CGB March  110.40 up 0.20   Volume 489 10-Yr Spread To U.S. 10-Yr 1.54 vs 1.58 "There's just been some position-squaring ahead of Christmas," said one trader at a domestic firm. The Canadian dollar was the focal point. After the Bank of Canada and the U.S. \par \par \uc2   Federal Reserve cut interest rates 25 basis points Tuesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been on a one-way tear higher. Thursday, the Canadian dollar rose to a high of US73.63 cents, after breaking US73.53 a couple of times. It was trading at US73.13 late Wednesday. That significant move forced the Bank of Canada to come in and buy U.S. dollars against the Canadian dollar to limit the rally. It's generally believed that the bank was not necessarily trying to reverse the strong trend in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but rather wants orderly markets during the thin pre-holiday sessions. Tuesday was the first time since the day after the Quebec sovereignty referendum that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been able to get any interest-rate relief into the economy. More bad news on the economy is expected Friday. It's anticipated that Statistics Canada will reveal that the Canadian economy actually contracted slightly in October. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) DOW JONES NEWS 12-21-95 \par \par \uc2  1635EST \par \par \uc2  4118 4152 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011024drcl02wuj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
