\par\par \b \uc2  Canadian Morning: Cdn Dlr Recovers From Early Weakness \b0\par\par\uc2 459 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Oktober 1995\par 15:42\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (AP-DJ)--The Canadian dollar continued lost ground in the early going Friday as more polls gave Quebec's separatists the edge in Monday's sovereignty referendum, but recovered slightly later. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar is trading at C$1.3723 at 1324 GMT, up from C$1.3720 at 1200 GMT and C$1.3700 late Thursday. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a high so far Friday around C$1.3775 shortly after the open. \par \par \uc2  'We had some stop-loss (U.S.) buy orders that sent (the U.S. dollar) up to highs, but it overshot and left a big vacuum, letting it slip back,' said another dealer with a large Canadian bank. \par \par \uc2  He said a large Swiss bank and other Swiss names were big sellers of Canada so far this session and that another test of the C$1.3780 area is very likely before the session is through. \par \par \uc2  After staging a comeback through the middle of the week, particularly following opinion polls suggesting momentum swinging back to the 'No' side in Quebec, the Canadian dollar resumed a downward spiral Thursday. An Angus Reid poll suggested voters will favor separation by a 52% to 48% margin. \par \par \uc2  A survey from the SOM polling firm released earlier today confirmed the trend with 46% of decided voters intending to vote for separation and 40% against. The poll had 10% of voters undecided. \par \par \uc2  A trader with a Canadian bank in New York said that with the poll numbers and weaker Canadian bonds, 'it can't look good for the (Canadian dollar) today.' Stronger than expected U.S. third quarter gross domestic product figures undermined the U.S. Treasury market and Canadian bonds, contributing to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  jitters in Canada. \par \par \uc2  A trader with a U.S. house in Toronto said there was some big buying of the Canadian dollar up around C$1.3780 that helped send it back to current levels. But other traders said there was no sign yet the Bank of Canada was in the market to support the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Many traders expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, and buy \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  should the U.S. dollar near the C$1.3800 level; a very likely possibility given pre-referendum jitters, they said. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the Environics daily tracking poll gave separatists 49% support and federalists 41% support with 10% undecided. The firm conducts the poll daily using a small sample size. \par \par \uc2  These were the exchange rates at 1324 GMT Friday, 1200 GMT and late Thursday. U.S./CDN         1.3723    1.3720    1.3700 CDN/Mark         1.0140    1.0153    1.0156 CDN/Yen          74.11     73.76     73.97 \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 27-10-95 \par \par \uc2  1342GMT \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025drar08fgo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
