\par\par \b \uc2  Canadian Afternoon: Cdn Dlr Falls Sharply Ahead Of Poll \b0\par\par\uc2 335 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Oktober 1995\par 22:17\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (AP-DJ)--The Canadian dollar was plunging toward new lows for the day late Friday, as players took a very cautious stand ahead of a weekend poll from the Montreal Groupe Leger & Leger, following sharp losses over the past couple sessions which prompted the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was trading at C$1.3530 at 2002 GMT, up from C$1.3439 at 1200 GMT and C$1.3420 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Traders have been reacting to a poll late Thursday that showed decided voters in Quebec in favor of separation by a margin of 45.4% to 43.6%. The poll had 11% of voters undecided, which, when divided proportionately, had 51% in favor of independence and 49% against. \par \par \uc2  One trader with a Canadian bank in New York said 'I think it's done,' referring to the sharp correction of the last 2 days. On Wednesday, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was getting around C$1.3380, and the Canadian dollar had weathered three other polls giving results similar to the Angus Reid poll. \par \par \uc2  But he too said that a lot now depends on what comes out of Saturday's Leger poll. If that shows even broader support for Quebec's separation from Canada, more severe losses can be expected on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Throughout midday, traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was buying Canadian dollars starting around the C$1.3475 level right up through C$1.3510, and was aiming to slow the losses. \par \par \uc2  But those efforts failed, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is now trading just below C$1.3535, a key level, according to economists with Path International, a market analytics firm. After that,  it could start heading for lows reached on Sept. 14, they write. The U.S. dollar traded at C$1.3738 then, as market players first discounted the potential for political turmoil stemming from the Quebec referendum. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 20-10-95 \par \par \uc2  2017GMT \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025drak0898j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
