\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Canada Intervention \highlight\uc2  -2-: Strong  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Tightens Conditions \b0\par\par\uc2 202 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Oktober 1995\par 16:15\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (AP-DJ)--The Bank of Canada bought U.S dollars around C$1.3280 early Tuesday, according to a trader with a large Canadian bank. The U.S. dollar had plunged through support levels around C$1.3340 overnight in Europe and broke the C$1.3300 figure early in the North American session, prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said traders. Each new strength in the Canadian dollar tightens up monetary conditions in Canada as measured by the widely watched monetary conditions index, a measure of the influence of interest rates and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the aggregate demand in the economy. But many think a very weak Canadian economy clearly warrants looser monetary conditions, and only the uncertainty deriving from the sovereignty campaign in Quebec hinders the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  from cutting official interest and loosening monetary policy. Quebecers will decide Oct. 30 whether or not to remain a part of Canada. \par \par \uc2  "So essentially all they can do is try to cool the rally in the Canadian dollar and keep conditions as easy as possible until after the referendum," said an analyst with a large bank in Toronto. \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES NEWS 10-03-95 \par \par \uc2  1015EDT \par \par \uc2  4020 4160 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011024dra3027pp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
