\par\par \b \uc2  Canadian Morning: Canadian Dlr Rides Wave Of  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 396 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 August 1995\par 16:06\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (AP-DJ)--The Canadian dollar is sharply higher against the U.S. dollar early Tuesday, riding the wave of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that has lifted the U.S. dollar to near-term highs against overseas \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar is trading at C$1.3574 at 1350 GMT, up from C$1.3598 at 1200 GMT and C$1.3613 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  Trading is heavy after a concerted efforts by the central banks of the U.S., Japan and Germany \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to propel the U.S dollar higher. The U.S. dollar is trading at 1.4720 marks and 96.55 yen after hitting highs earlier of 1.4750 and 96.83 respectively. \par \par \uc2  Once again, central banks \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the U.S. dollar was strengthening, and many analysts believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will benefit strongly from the latest round. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar started gaining ground after Japan reported a 23% reduction in its trade surplus with the rest of the world, with exports to the U.S. falling for the first time in almost three years. The surplus with the U.S. shrunk by 31% to $3.87 billion. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan started building on this strength and began \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in favor of the U.S. dollar, boosting it higher before the Bundesbank and Fed joined in. \par \par \uc2  After trading in a fairly narrow range during the Asian and European sessions, the Canadian dollar shot up as trading opened in Toronto. \par \par \uc2  'It was a bit of a delayed reaction,' said one New York-based trader, adding that players began turning their eyes towards Canada as it benefitted from a 'Buy North America' sentiment. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the Canadian dollar is rising on heavy cross activity, as the U.S. dollar continues to push higher. The U.S. dollar weakened quickly, moving from an intraday high of C$1.3620 at 1000 GMT to a low of C$1.3545 at 1300 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Apparently, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not among the central banks \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  These are \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates at 1350 GMT Tuesday, at 1200 GMT and late Monday. U.S./CDN         1.3574     1.3598    1.3613 CDN/Mark         1.0844     1.0650    1.0541 CDN/Yen          71.24      69.96     68.78 \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 15-08-95 \par \par \uc2  1406GMT \par \par \uc2  (Corrected 1424GMT) \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr8f066gp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
