\par\par \b \uc2  Canadian Bonds -2-: Rate Move Seen Possible, But Unlikely \b0\par\par\uc2 371 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 August 1995\par 17:13\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  However, J.P. Morgan's Carmichael says the net impact of events so far this morning favors the negative side for bonds. The stronger dollar is good for bonds, clearly, but the comments from the Fed's Blinder carry a great deal of weight. In Canada, meanwhile, little has changed fundamentally. July leading indicators fell 0.3% from June, underlining still sluggish growth in the economy and supporting the view that the Bank of Canada will use every opportunity to cut interest rates. Still, the referendum campaign in Quebec is expected to produce volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and credit markets in Canada, and some believe that could result in a defensive tightening of monetary conditions at some point. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  "would like to start (that) from a lower point," says John Johnston. deputy chief economist with the Royal Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will use the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 -derived strength of the Canadian dollar to ease its call loan target again is unclear, but seen unlikely. The Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already lost some strength since \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  started, with the U.S. dollar now trading back around C$1.3600 after touching support at C$1.3545 earlier. Late Monday, it traded at C$1.3613. Economists say central bankers are keen for another opportunity to lower rates and a move can't be ruled out. Many observers thought last week's rate move was a wily one, and Johnston says that if money-market rates ease a touch and the Canadian dollar strengthens a bit the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could use the opportunity to lower the call loan target another 1/4 point. Because the German Bundesbank is likely to ease its repo rate in the next few weeks, and in light of the Blinder comments pointing to neutral policy, the outlook for the U.S. and Canadian dollars has improved and another Canadian rate cut would not be completely out of line at his point, he says. In the money market, the three-month rate is steady at 6.53%-6.51% and the call loan trades at mid-range. \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES NEWS 08-15-95 \par \par \uc2  1113EDT \par \par \uc2  4020 4152 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011024dr8f01wvc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
