\par\par \b \uc2  CDN Afternoon: Battered Cdn Dlr Prompts BOC  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 358 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juli 1995\par 22:03\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (AP-DJ)--The Canadian dollar suffered its first bout of real weakness since it began its move higher near the end of June, traders said. It lost considerable ground Thursday against the U.S. dollar, forcing the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOC) to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to moderate its decline. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is trading at C$1.3619 at 1945 GMT, up from C$1.3527 at 1200 GMT and C$1.3553 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  'It's taking a beating,' said one trader, adding that 'it's been a one-way traffic to sell the Canadian dollar.' \par \par \uc2  A market source said the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  began \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  around 1500 GMT at C$1.3525, as the U.S. dollar moved toward its intraday high of C$1.3645 at 1750 GMT. The U.S. dollar traded between C$1.3515 and C$1.3645, seeing its widest one-day swing since early May, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar had entered the North American session strongly Thursday morning, after a cut in Swiss interest rates drove European investors to Canadian dollars. \par \par \uc2  But when the German \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to take a similar rate action, traders said investors began selling everything against the German mark. \par \par \uc2  The sharp drop in the Canadian dollar took some traders by surprise, who were expecting the U.S. dollar to meet resistance at the C$1.3570 area. 'I don't think there's anything really behind (the weakness),' said one trader. \par \par \uc2  Douglas Porter, senior economist at Bank of Nova Scotia, said the Canadian dollar is suffering a fallout, in part, from the slumping U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  'As easy as it went up last week, it's now coming down,' said Porter, adding there have been no economic fundamentals responsible for any change in sentiment toward the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  These are the rates at 1930 GMT and 1200 GMT Thursday, and late Wednesday. U.S./CDN     1.3619   1.3527   1.3553 CDN/Mark     1.0199   1.0410   1.0346 CDN/Yen      64.18    65.23    64.49 \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 13-07-95 \par \par \uc2  2003GMT \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr7d058lj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
