\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of Canada Reverses -2-: Eases Policy After Weak US Data \b0\par\par\uc2 365 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juni 1995\par 15:29\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (AP-DJ)-- The Bank of Canada did a round of reverse sale and repurchase agreements at 7%, signalling an easing in monetary policy after more weak U.S. economic data showed signs \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 's major export market is in trouble. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  cuts the bank's overnight lending rate 25 basis points to trade between 7% and 7.5%. The Canadian dollar is weakening slightly after the rate cut. It's trading at US72.25 cents compared with US72.54 cents late Monday. "Because of the weak GDP numbers Monday and signs that U.S. domestic demand has continued sluggish means that Canada is going to follow suit," said Michael Gregory, economist with Lehman Brothers Canada Inc. The Commerce Department said retail sales in the U.S. rose by 0.2% in May, far below expectations of a gain of 0.8%. That followed data Monday from Canada showing its gross domestic product grew by only 0.7% at an annualized rate in the first quarter of 1995 compared to growth of 4.6% in the fourth quarter of 1994. \par \par \uc2   Some economists are now predicting negative growth in Canada in the second quarter. Economists have been calling for an easing in monetary policy to keep Canada from slipping into recession. It's the third time the Bank of Canada has lowered its overnight rate by 25 basis points in the past two months, and all have followed very weak U.S. economic numbers. Although many analysts had believed the Bank of Canada would not lower rates without a similar move by the Federal Reserve, the slew of bad economic numbers coming out of the U.S. has all but ruled out an interest-rate increase by the Fed. That enables the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to lower rates measuredly without narrowing too significantly the interest-rate spread Canada needs to keep investors attracted to its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Tuesday's retail sales data are likely to intensify the call on Fed chairman Alan Greenspan to cut the federal funds rate from its current level of 6%. \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES NEWS 06-13-95 \par \par \uc2  0929EDT \par \par \uc2  4020 4160 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011024dr6d01fxj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
