\par\par \b \uc2  =Canadian Bonds -2-: Downgrade Would Be Bad News For Market \b0\par\par\uc2 315 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Februar 1995\par 23:26\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Barry Allan, vice president of fixed income investments at Altamira Management Service, Toronto, said the timing of the Moody's announcement came as a surprise to the financial markets, and seemed to indicate that Moody's is setting the stage for a downgrade in the weeks ahead. Like most money managers, Allan said a downgrade of Canadian debt would hurt the market's prospects for attracting new investors and holding onto existing ones. Indeed, the Canadian bond market ended sharply lower despite the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate action. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  with a round of reverse sale and repurchase agreements at 7.75%, according to a money-market sources. The action, in effect, set a new floor for overnight interest rates. The new target range is 7.75% to 8.25%, up from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's previous target range of 7.25% to 7.75%. \par \par \uc2  Paul Ferely, assistant chief economist at Bank of Montreal, said the increase in the call loan rate was consistent with the Bank of Canada's aggressive attempts in recent weeks to protect the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and restore calm to North American financial markets. "The strategy now is to shore up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  whenever they can," Ferely said. In a press release, Moody's said that although there have been some improvements in Canada's overall public sector deficits, both at the federal and provincial levels, it is concerned about the medium-term deficit outlook, especially as regards the prospects facing Canada's public sector once the next, inevitable, economic downturn occurs. Moody's said it will explore the risks that federal and provincial deficits pose to Canada's medium-term credit position, in light of the structurally heightened volatility witnessed in international capital markets in the recent past. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) DOW JONES NEWS 02-16-95 \par \par \uc2  1726EST \par \par \uc2  4020 4238 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011024dr2g00pmg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
