\par\par \b \uc2  CDN Afternoon: CDN Dlr Stronger On IMM Buying \b0\par\par\uc2 360 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Februar 1995\par 22:07\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  1/8o-dji r/cn \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (AP-DJ)--The Canadian dollar strengthened Monday in North America from levels seen Friday after buying on Chicago's IMM exchange pushed it up through technical resistance levels. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was trading at 1.3966 CDN dlrs around 2050 GMT Monday, down from 1.4001 CDN dlrs at 1300 GMT, when North American trading began, and down from 1.4026 CDN dlrs late Friday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar hit spot lows of 1.3938 CDN dlrs late Monday after its fall below a technical support level at 1.3955 CDN dlrs sparked stop-loss buying of Canadian dollars. Traders say this technical trading was behind strong demand for Canadian dollars late Monday on the IMM, a part of the Chicago Mercantile Exchange. \par \par \uc2  Early in the session there was inter-bank demand for Canadian dollars, in exchange for Deutsche marks and Japanese yen, with strong U.S. dollar selling coming in later. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Canada reportedly bought U.S. dollars early in the session at levels around 1.3960 CDN dlrs, a move that traders said was aimed at rebuilding reserves and smoothing trading. There were no confirmed Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  late Monday, after the U.S. dollar broke below 1.3955 CDN dlrs, but traders say the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have been in the market discreetly, through just one dealer. \par \par \uc2  Heading into Tuesday's session, traders expect the U.S. dollar will find support at 1.3940 CDN dlrs and resistance at 1.3970 CDN dlrs. \par \par \uc2  There was no major Canadian economic news Monday. There is a 6.2 billion CDN dlrs treasury bill auction Tuesday. The Bank of Canada bank rate will be set after the auction and is expected to decline by 17 basis points. \par \par \uc2  These are \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates in Toronto at 2105 GMT Monday compared with rates at 1300 GMT and late Friday. U.S./CDN               1.3966     1.4001     1.4026 CDN/Mark               1.0971     1.0940     1.0901 CDN/Yen                 71.20      71.11      70.26 \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 06-02-95 \par \par \uc2  2107GMT \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr2600skh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
