\par\par \b \uc2  CDN Bonds Mixed, Drifting Ahead Of FOMC Meeting Tuesday \b0\par\par\uc2 431 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Januar 1995\par 16:24\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (AP-DJ)--The Canadian bond market has turned tentative early Tuesday, with prices drifting slightly higher in most maturities but little trading taking place as two days of policy-making meetings begin later Tuesday for the Federal Reserve Board. ISSUE       PRICE  CHANGE   YIELD 7.75s 1996  98.40  UNCH     8.79% 8.5s  2000  97.20  Up 0.10  9.17% 9.0s  2004  97.90  Up 0.20  9.31% 9s    2025  96.40  Up 0.20  9.36% CGB March   97.73  Up 0.07 10-Yr Spread To U.S. 10-Yr 1.67 vs 1.71 "The strength of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has pulled this market back after it drifted down overnight," says a Toronto-based trader. But he says little account interest in bonds is expected with the Federal Reserve's Open Market Committee meeting until Wednesday and a key U.S. employment report due Friday. The U.S. dollar is changing hands at $1.4155 (Canadian) early Tuesday compared with C$1.4195 late Monday. There is a C$1.9 billion auction of government of Canada 9s of 2004 bonds on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2   Although demand for the bonds might be subdued due to the FOMC meeting and the flat yield curve, one trader says, "the street's going to do its best to cheapen up the issue, and there's decent natural demand for the 10-year bonds, so the auction may actually work out well." In the money market Tuesday, traders say the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the fourth consecutive session to cap an upward trend in overnight rates and establish its own target range of 6.75% to 7.25% for overnight money. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was reportedly doing special purchase and resale agreements early Tuesday at 7.25% to set a ceiling on rates. There is a C$6.3 billion treasury bill auction Tuesday, and the Bank of Canada bank rate will be set following the T-bill sale. There is C$6.55 billion in T-bills maturing. Based on yields in the when-issued market for T-bills, the Bank of Canada bank rate will drop five basis points Tuesday to 8.33% from 8.38% at last week's setting. In Canadian economic news, the gross domestic product rose 0.4% in November from October, led by a strong gain in manufacturing. This report was in line with economists' expectations and had little influence on bond trading. \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES NEWS 01-31-95 \par \par \uc2  1024EST \par \par \uc2  4020 4118 4152 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011024dr1v00kyw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
