\par\par \b \uc2  CDN Afternoon: CDN Dlr Stronger In Inter-Bank Trading \b0\par\par\uc2 417 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Januar 1995\par 22:03\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (AP-DJ)--The Canadian dollar rebounded from early weakness in Wednesday's session in North America but remains below levels seen late Tuesday after major banks came in as buyers of the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  when it bounced off a major technical barrier. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was trading at 1.4110 CDN dlrs around 2045 GMT Wednesday, down slightly from 1.4120 CDN dlrs at 1300 GMT, when North American trading began, but up from 1.4100 CDN dlrs late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar hit spot highs of 1.4140 CDN dlrs Wednesday for the second consecutive session, but traders say there was no sign of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was reportedly selling U.S. dollars Tuesday to smooth Canadian dollar trading. \par \par \uc2  The 1.4140 CDN dlr level represents an important technical barrier for the U.S. dollar; it's a nine-year high. Failure to break higher put selling pressure on the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  'We got a little overdone, and just like in Tuesday's session, there was inter-bank interest in moving Canada back a bit,' says a Toronto-based \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader. \par \par \uc2  Traders say inter-bank trading may take the U.S. dollar below 1.4100 CDN dlrs heading into Thursday's session, and a trading range with support at 1.4080 CDN dlrs and resistance at 1.4120 CDN dlrs is expected. There is no major Canadian economic news Thursday. \par \par \uc2  But overall market sentiment is still bearish on the Canadian dollar, despite the Bank of Canada's 50 basis point hike Tuesday in overnight rates. That move took the Canadian call loan target rate to a band between 5.75% and 6.25%. A report Wednesday from Toronto Dominion Securities Inc. says, 'the Bank of Canada's tightening of the call loan target is likely to be viewed as too little, too late. Market expectations are set for another run at weaker levels.' \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar is expected to come under pressure towards the end of the January, as market participants anticipate further hikes in the U.S. federal fund target rate. \par \par \uc2  These are \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates in Toronto at 2045 GMT Wednesday compared with rates at 1300 GMT and late Tuesday. U.S./CDN               1.4110      1.4120     1.4100 CDN/Mark               1.0884      1.0887     1.0867 CDN/Yen                 70.76       70.82      70.92 \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 11-01-95 \par \par \uc2  2103GMT \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr1b004ai\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
