\par\par \b \uc2  CDN Dlr Weaker Despite  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 , Rate Hike \b0\par\par\uc2 541 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Januar 1995\par 17:44\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (AP-DJ)--A hike in the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2 's overnight interest rate target and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to stop a sharp drop in the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday. The Canadian dollar is at a 9-year low against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  At late morning, the Canadian dollar is sharply weaker than earlier North American levels and well below those seen late Monday. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar is being undermined by concerns over the Quebec independence movement and the federal government's fiscal woes. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was trading at 1.4130 CDN dlrs around 1625 GMT Tuesday, up from 1.4088 CDN dlrs at 1300 GMT, when North American trading began, and up from 1.4086 CDN dlrs late Monday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar hit spot highs of 1.4140 CDN dlrs in Tuesday's session, a level not seen since March 6, 1986 when the U.S. dollar hit 1.4160 CDN dlrs. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Canada used reverse sale and repurchase agreements Tuesday at 5.75% to signal a hike in its target call loan rate. The Bank of Canada is seen Tuesday as defending a call loan target rate of 5.75% to 6.25%, compared with a band of 5.25% to 5.75% that was in place going into Tuesday's session. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Canada was also reported to be selling U.S. dollars at levels above 1.4105 CDN dlrs to smooth the sharp weakening in the Canadian dollar. \par \par \uc2  'You would think there'd be a positive reaction to the hike in the call loan rate, but we haven't seen it,' says a Toronto-based trader. He says the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seen as trying to set a premium above the 5.5% U.S. federal funds target rate. \par \par \uc2  But traders say if the U.S. dollar stays below 1.4135 CDN dlrs through the session, there will likely be a retracement of part of Tuesday's move on profit-taking by banks and funds. The U.S. dollar is expected to find support at 1.4110 CDN dlrs and resistance at 1.4135 CDN dlrs in Tuesday's session. \par \par \uc2  Overall, sentment continues to be negative, with many economists expecting a test of 1.4200 CDN dlrs. \par \par \uc2  Market participants are comparing Canada's high debt levels to those of Sweden, where a budget was tabled on Tuesday. One trader noted, 'The Swedes came out with a fairly draconian budget and the market has continued to pummel the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Perhaps we in Canada should sit up and take notice.' \par \par \uc2  Canada's federal Liberal government is expected to unveil its budget in late February. \par \par \uc2  In Canadian economic news, new car sales fell 4.3% in November from October. Analysts surveyed by Technical Data forecast a 1.2% increase in November sales. Traders say the report had no influence on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading. \par \par \uc2  These are \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates in Toronto at 1625 GMT Tuesday compared with rates at 1300 GMT and late Monday. U.S./CDN               1.4130      1.4088     1.4086 CDN/Mark               1.0896      1.0910     1.0916 CDN/Yen                 71.16       71.15      70.93 \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 10-01-95 \par \par \uc2  1644GMT \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr1a002rd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
