\par\par \b \uc2  CDN Morning: CDN Dlr Weakens On Quebec Polls \b0\par\par\uc2 338 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Januar 1995\par 16:34\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TORONTO (AP-DJ)--The Canadian dollar is weaker early Monday in North America and is below late-Friday levels in part due to a poll from Quebec showing a sharp rise in support for independence. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was trading at 1.4040 CDN dlrs around 1505 GMT Monday, up from 1.4028 CDN dlrs at 1300 GMT when North American trading began and up from 1.3995 CDN dlrs late Friday. \par \par \uc2  A poll released early Monday shows 47% of Quebecers support sovereignty, up from 41% in a previous polls. Economists with MMS International downplayed the results, saying the sample size is small. \par \par \uc2  'This is just the first of many polls that are going to shake out any weak Canadian postions. Trading is actually very quiet,' says a Toronto-based trader. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar is expected to trade Monday in a range with support at 1.4020 CDN dlrs and resistance at 1.4060 CDN dlrs. \par \par \uc2  The weakening Mexican peso is again the subject of international attention, with the New York Federal Reserve Bank buying pesos against the U.S. dollar at the request of Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Banco de Mexico. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Canada\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not part of this \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to Canadian traders. \par \par \uc2  The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has drawn down 83 million CDN dlrs of a swap facility with Canada. The swap facility is for 1.0 billion CDN dlrs. The Banco de Mexico has also drawn 500 million U.S. dlrs against its swap facility with the Federal Reserve. This activity is not expected to influence spot trading in Canadian dollars. \par \par \uc2  There are no major Canadian economic news on Monday. \par \par \uc2  These are \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates in Toronto at 1505 GMT Monday compared with rates at 1300 GMT and late Friday. U.S./CDN               1.4040      1.4028     1.3995 CDN/Mark               1.1090      1.1108     1.1163 CDN/Yen                 71.83       71.89      72.37 \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 09-01-95 \par \par \uc2  1534GMT \par \par \uc2  1158 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr190020l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
